# Docker Standards

## Base images
- Pin versions — `FROM node:22.12-alpine3.21`, never `:latest`. Prefer minimal official images (alpine/slim variants).
- One concern per container; split web app, database, cache, and workers into separate services.

## Dockerfile
- Multi-stage builds: build stage with toolchain, slim runtime stage that copies only artifacts.
- Order instructions least → most frequently changing to maximize layer-cache hits: copy dependency manifests, install, then copy source.

```dockerfile
# ✅ GOOD — cache survives source changes
COPY package.json pnpm-lock.yaml ./
RUN pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
COPY . .
```

- Combine `apt-get update` and install in one `RUN` with `--no-install-recommends`, sort packages alphabetically, clean up `/var/lib/apt/lists/*` in the same layer.
- `ARG` for build-time values, `ENV` for runtime values; `WORKDIR` with absolute paths instead of `RUN cd`.
- `COPY` over `ADD` (use `ADD` only for remote artifacts with `--checksum`).
- Run as non-root: create a user, `chown` app files, `USER appuser` before `CMD`.
- `HEALTHCHECK` on every long-running service.
- Always ship a `.dockerignore` (`.git`, `node_modules`, `.env*`, logs, test artifacts).

## Production vs development images
- Never bake test, lint, or debugger tools into the production final stage — profiles do not strip packages already installed in a shared image.
- Prefer one Dockerfile with stages `base` → `production` / `development`, selected via Compose `build.target`. Use separate `Dockerfile` / `Dockerfile.dev` only when the process model differs (e.g. nginx vs Next/Vite).
- Compose selects the path with `profiles: [production]` / `profiles: [dev]` and/or `build.target`.
- Bind-mount source only on the development path; production images copy built artifacts only (no live mounts of app source).

## entrypoint.sh
- Start with `#!/bin/sh` (or bash) and `set -e`; end with `exec "$@"` so the app becomes PID 1 and receives signals.
- Entrypoints do setup only (migrations, waiting for deps, permissions) — no business logic.

## Compose
- Named volumes for persistence; bind mounts only for development.
- Services talk via service names on the default/custom bridge network — never `network_mode: host`, never hardcoded container IPs.
- Startup ordering via `depends_on` with `condition: service_healthy`, not sleep hacks.
- Configuration via environment variables with defaults (`${VAR:-default}`); secrets come from `.env` (gitignored) or compose `secrets:` — never hardcoded in the file.
- Logs go to stdout/stderr; never write log files inside the container.
